WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:07.750
One more thing comes with the license: drug and alcohol rules that are stricter than for any recreational boater.

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.550
As a commercial operator, you must be enrolled in a Department of Transportation drug testing program.

3
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:18.875
Most owner-operators join a consortium that handles it.

4
00:00:19.125 --> 00:00:26.450
The tests come before employment, at random, after a serious marine incident, and when there’s reasonable cause.

5
00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:32.850
For alcohol, a commercial operator is intoxicated at zero point zero four percent.

6
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.575
That’s half the recreational limit.

7
00:00:35.825 --> 00:00:39.275
After a serious marine incident, the clock starts.

8
00:00:39.525 --> 00:00:44.575
Alcohol testing within two hours, drug testing within thirty-two hours.

9
00:00:44.825 --> 00:00:48.050
And refusing a test can cost you your license.

10
00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:50.875
That’s lesson one.

11
00:00:51.125 --> 00:00:54.875
Six passengers, uninspected vessel, five years.

12
00:00:55.125 --> 00:00:58.750
If they have to pay to come, they’re passengers for hire.

13
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:03.025
And zero point zero four, two hours, thirty-two hours.

14
00:01:03.275 --> 00:01:07.175
Next time: the safety gear the law requires on your boat.
